title: Claude Code's transcripts record what each session and subagent spent, with gaps.
pid: e12537a4-e5a9-4d75-b6c8-713f5589be8d
body: |2-
  Every session's tokens, model and times are in Claude Code's
  transcripts, '.jsonl' files under 'my-dot-claude/projects/'.
  'tools/team/spending_account.py' reads them into two tables in
  'data/claude/spending/': 'account.tsv', a row per session and per
  subagent, and 'requests.tsv', a row per API request, which join on
  'id'. The pacer runs it after each session it starts. Its help says
  how to run it, what each column means, how the price and the weighted
  price are made, and how to query both. What the code cannot say
  cheaply is below.
contains:
- b7d2e829-b9d5-40ff-bd01-fac1a0d408f5
